# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `marker_mismatch`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: a value that is no place, handed to an `@` parameter, is held in a temporary the callee writes and nobody reads, so the write falls.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w27-marker_mismatch-non-place), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

function bump(@n: i64)
    n @ n + 1

function main()
    bump(1)  #~ marker_mismatch
    print(2)
